{"id":2027,"date":"2017-04-11T17:16:39","date_gmt":"2017-04-12T00:16:39","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/?p=2027"},"modified":"2017-04-11T17:16:39","modified_gmt":"2017-04-12T00:16:39","slug":"results-of-uc-berkeley-ve-session-on-march-15-2017","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/2017\/04\/11\/results-of-uc-berkeley-ve-session-on-march-15-2017\/","title":{"rendered":"Results of UC Berkeley VE Session on March 15, 2017"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Reported by Randy Jenkins KA6BQF<\/p>\n<p><span title=\"ka6bqf@gmail.com\">ka6bqf@gmail.com<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">On March 15, 2017 there was a VE Session at UC Berkeley.<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">\u00a0 <\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">There were 74 candidates registered, our team of 11 VE\u2019s welcomed 66 candidates, including three upgrades, and 63 new licensees.<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">\u00a0 <\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">62 candidates were successful in getting their initial license.<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">\u00a0 <\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">The three candidates for license upgrades were successful. 65 successful candidates. <\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">The team administered <\/span>a total of 86 exam elements. The test elements administered (P\/F) are; Technician 61\/1, General 9\/8, and Extra 4\/3.\u00a0 There were 55 new Technician, 6 General, and 4 Extra licenses, awarded.\u00a0<span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">There were students and staff from the Cal Electrical Engineering Department and the Cal Solar Car Team.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">Some VE\u2019s on the team drove from Petaluma, Novato, and San Francisco.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Reported by Randy Jenkins KA6BQF ka6bqf@gmail.com On March 15, 2017 there was a VE Session at UC Berkeley.\u00a0 There were 74 candidates registered, our team of 11 VE\u2019s welcomed 66 <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"http:\/\/ccra.us\/2017\/04\/11\/results-of-uc-berkeley-ve-session-on-march-15-2017\/\">Continue Reading &rarr;<\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_jetpack_newsletter_access":"","_jetpack_dont_email_post_to_subs":false,"_jetpack_newsletter_tier_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paywalled_content":false,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paid_content":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[2],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-2027","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-ccra-news"],"jetpack_featured_media_url":"","jetpack_sharing_enabled":true,"jetpack_shortlink":"https:\/\/wp.me\/p69ory-wH","_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2027","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2027"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2027\/revisions"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2027"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=202